span>Modules</span></span></a></div></li><li class="documentation-sidebar__list-item"><div class="documentation-sidebar__item" style="padding-left:16px"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link" href="same-height"><span class="documentation-sidebar__link-content"><span>Same height</span></span></a></div></li><li class="documentation-sidebar__list-item"><div class="documentation-sidebar__item" style="padding-left:16px"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link documentation-sidebar__link--active" href="toggle"><span class="documentation-sidebar__link-content"><span>Toggle</span></span></a></div></li></ul></li></ul></nav><div class="documentation-sidebar__version"><a class="documentation-sidebar__link" href="../changelog">v<!-- -->3.4.0</a></div></aside><main class="documentation-sidebar__content"><h1 class="bold" id="toggle"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="toggle#toggle">Toggle</a></h1>
<p>Toggle is a handy module used for toggling attribute values, class names, text content and icons on any element with a click.</p>
<p>To start toggling, you need a trigger and a target (or multiple targets). Settings are passed into <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">data-toggle</span></span></code></span> attribute of the trigger element as an array of objects. Each setting object holds information about how to find targets, which attribute should be toggled and a new value.</p>
